From 2f2f344f1754bd04d8451a6741e394cdb8d74927 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 19:22:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0138 -- wave-43 RUNMANIFEST schema-v1
 emit

flush-instr's wave-41 tri-env correlation framework (per
docs/internal/WAVE-41-TRI-ENV-CORRELATION-PLAN.md sec. 4) defines an
18-field RUNMANIFEST schema-v1 block that every instrumented binary
emits at end of clean exit. This patch wires DOSKUTSU.EXE's emit.
HWINV.EXE-side emit was authored by probe-engineer task #10/#16.
Shared header at `include/runmanifest.h` (probe-engineer task #16);
this patch consumes it.

Schema fields populated per spec sec. 4.2 (those in the engine's
purview at MVP):
- schema_version=1 (constant)
- environment={dosbox-x|86box|realhw|unknown} via 3-state auto-detect
  (CPUID hypervisor + INT 21h AX=4452h AND-gate for DOSBox-X; 86Box
  BIOS-string scan at F000:E000-FFFF for 86Box; DOSKUTSU_ENVIRONMENT
  env var as belt-and-suspenders override per probe-engineer's
  recommendation for cross-binary consistency)
- binary_sha12 = compile-time git short-SHA stamp via Makefile
  -DDOSKUTSU_BUILD_SHA12 (bare token; C preprocessor stringifies
  via _DOSKUTSU_STR macro)
- wave_tag from existing DOSKUTSU_LOG_TAG env var
- scene from new DOSKUTSU_SCENE_TAG env var (operator sets per-BAT)
- env_block_sha12 = runmanifest_compute_env_block_sha12() over a
  30-entry pre-sorted alphabetical allowlist (DOSKUTSU_TAS_*,
  SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_*, BLASTER, DOSKUTSU_LOG_TAG, DOSKUTSU_SCENE_TAG)
- started_utc captured in main() at very start via std::time + gmtime
  + strftime ISO8601
- duration_s = std::time(nullptr) - _runmanifest_boot_time at emit
- exit_code = 0 on clean shutdown path (ingame_error: sets error=true
  but goto-jumps through this code path -- MVP emits 0 since reaching
  here means we made it through engine teardown without abort)

Schema fields populated NA per spec (perf-vital pass-throughs filled
by future wave-42-iter04+ work per docs/internal/WAVE-41-PERF-LOGGING-
PLAN.md sec. 7):
- fps_p50, fps_p95: emit NA via runmanifest_init() default sentinels
- audio_vital_status, regime: emit NA via NULL pointer defaults

Schema fields placeholder per spec (smoke gate post-processes via grep):
- banner_required_hit / _total / _forbidden / _optional: 0
- critical_count / warn_count: 0

Hook point: after engine-shutdown[final] doskutsu_dbg_log + before
return from main(). All teardown complete + Logger djgpp_log_fp still
open (closes implicitly at process exit). emit_run_manifest() is a
static file-scope function; single call site; pure side-effect on
djgpp_log_fp. Per-line fsync after emit per [[sdl3_dos_quirks]]
DEBUG.LOG-fsync precedent.

Boot wall-clock captured at FIRST line of main() via static-file-
scope std::time_t _runmanifest_boot_time so the duration_s field is
process-lifetime (not engine-init-to-shutdown which would miss the
Logger::init + SDL_Init prelude).

Two-witness banner: LOG_INFO "[runmanifest-emit] schema=v{} env={}
sha12={} dur={}s tag='{}' scene='{}' env_sha={} (signals=0x{:x})"
fires after the bracketed block. Allows smoke gate to verify runtime
emit happened (separate from strings|grep `RUNMANIFEST-BEGIN` which
only proves embed).

Default-OFF: emit happens unconditionally on clean shutdown (NOT
env-var-gated). Rationale: RUNMANIFEST is instrumentation that
benefits ALL iters, has zero perf cost at runtime (one fsync at
exit; immeasurable vs the ~1-2 sec engine-shutdown sequence
overall), and the no-env-block-sha case is harmless (env_block_sha
just hashes an empty allowlist match). Smoke gates can ignore the
block if they don't consume the manifest. Per
[[single_lever_per_binary_or_else_attribution_impossible]]: this is
INSTRUMENTATION (not an fps lever); attribution preserved.

Build-flag additions in top-level Makefile (RUNMANIFEST_FLAGS):
- -I${REPO_ROOT}/include: lets engine TU find runmanifest.h without
  modifying vendored CMakeLists.txt; harmless to other build stages
  since they don't #include it
- -DDOSKUTSU_BUILD_SHA12=<bare-token>: passes git short SHA at
  make-config time as a bare C identifier token; main.cpp's _DOSKUTSU_
  STR macro stringifies via C preprocessor. Avoids the multi-layer
  quote-escape pain through bash + make + cmake -> compiler -D
  forwarding. Fallback "UNKNOWN_____" (12 chars; pads sha12 field)
  if git unavailable.

Files:
  src/main.cpp  -- include runmanifest.h, file-scope boot-time
                   static + allowlist + emit fn (~150 lines added),
                   2 call sites (boot capture in main() entry + emit
                   call before return error;)

CMakeLists.txt unchanged (no new .cpp files; emit fn is in main.cpp).

docs/BOOT.md entries for DOSKUTSU_ENVIRONMENT + DOSKUTSU_SCENE_TAG
land in parent doskutsu repo (not vendor commit) per
[[env_vars_document_in_user_docs]].

tools/dosbox-x.conf + tools/dosbox-x-fast.conf will add
`SET DOSKUTSU_ENVIRONMENT=dosbox-x` to their autoexec sections so
smoke runs self-identify as dosbox-x (separate parent-repo change;
not in vendor commit).
